    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7H7pGe",
      "title": "Update addGameType and setDisputeGame templates",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1378,
      "body": "Updates addGameType and setDisputeGame templates after U18 OPCM breaking changes:\r\n\r\n## OPCM Changes for Superchain-Ops\r\n\r\nU18 introduces a couple breaking changes to OPCM. They can be summarized by the following changes:\r\n\r\n1. Implied ProxyAdmin inputs. The proxy admin is no longer a salient input to execute opcm operations. Instead, OPCM will retrieve the proxy admin from the system config.\r\n2. Cannon Kona prestates. This is a new required input for some dispute game related operations.\r\n\r\n### addGameType\r\n\r\nThe `proxyAdmin` is no longer an input to the `AddGameInput` struct as was the case before U18. The new input set follows:\r\n\r\n```less\r\nstruct AddGameInput {\r\n        string saltMixer;\r\n        ISystemConfig systemConfig;\r\n        IDelayedWETH delayedWETH;\r\n        GameType disputeGameType;\r\n        Claim disputeAbsolutePrestate;\r\n        uint256 disputeMaxGameDepth;\r\n        uint256 disputeSplitDepth;\r\n        Duration disputeClockExtension;\r\n        Duration disputeMaxClockDuration;\r\n        uint256 initialBond;\r\n        IBigStepper vm;\r\n        bool permissioned;\r\n }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe current [[AddGameType template](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/blob/4b25d9ed5e2c52c111fdb3e7393dcc18393334b4/src/template/AddGameTypeTemplate.sol#L31C2-L46C6)](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/blob/4b25d9ed5e2c52c111fdb3e7393dcc18393334b4/src/template/AddGameTypeTemplate.sol#L31C2-L46C6) uses the pre-U18 struct that includes the proxyAdmin. It should be updated to omit the proxyAdmin.\r\n\r\n### updatePrestate\r\n\r\nPrior to U18, `updatePrestate` required a set of `OPChainConfig` structs. For U18, the input has been changed to an array of `UpdatePrestateInput`:\r\n\r\n```less\r\n    struct UpdatePrestateInput {\r\n        ISystemConfig systemConfigProxy;\r\n        Claim cannonPrestate;\r\n        Claim cannonKonaPrestate;\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor reference, here’s the updated ABI in OPCM - https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/eed603f0c35969cc85624381e0449df772ef3d24/packages/contracts-bedrock/src/L1/OPContractsManager.sol#L758\r\n\r\n<aside>\r\n💡\r\n\r\nBoth the cannonPrestate AND cannonKonaPrestate must be non-zero when specifying the UpdatePrestateInput\r\n\r\n</aside>\r\n\r\n## upgrade\r\n\r\nThe set of `OpChainConfig` inputs provided to the `upgrade` function has been changed to the following:\r\n\r\n```less\r\n   struct OpChainConfig {\r\n        ISystemConfig systemConfigProxy;\r\n        Claim cannonPrestate;\r\n        Claim cannonKonaPrestate;\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe changes include:\r\n\r\n- `proxyAdmin` removed from the struct\r\n- `cannonKonaPrestate` added\r\n- the previously named `absolutePrestate` was renamed to `cannonPrestate`.\r\n\r\n## Other potential superchain-ops changes\r\n\r\n### `SetDisputeGameImpl`\r\n\r\nI’m unsure when or how this task template is used. But as it stands, it’s no longer compatible with U18. This is because in order to set a dispute game implementation in the factory, you must now also provide “game arguments”. The game args are a set of fixed game configurations that were previously provided in the FaultDisputeGame constructor. They’ve been moved to a separate storage to make the dispute game contracts MCP compatible.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
